{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings","id":767450,"title":"How have the Deathlords not won? (Ex3 Solar Sorcerous Workings)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-16T17:14:27-08:00","id":767450,"title":"How have the Deathlords not won? (Ex3 Solar Sorcerous Workings)","content":"Abyssals, presumably, can get at least Celestial Circle Sorcery. IIRC 2e Deathlords could have it themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Ambition 3. </b><br /> * Change a fundamental rule of the cosmos such that the air is made of lava.<br /> * Shut off Creation's reincarnation process and let things sort itself out.<br /> * Everyone that dies becomes a Nephwrack in service to the Neverborn.<br /> * Everyone that dies becomes Chejop Kejack.<br /> * Have the Void come alive and just eat everything Galacticus style.'<br /> * Sickness spreads like crazy and can not be cured.<br /> * All attempts at social interaction physically harm people.<br /> * Etc. Etc. Etc.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 11-16-2015, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:17:12-08:00","id":767452,"title":"","content":"It's not like we got Charms in Ex3 by which Solar Circle Workings were rendered trivial, and even if we had, we've already been told Ex3 Deathlords don't use Solar Charms. Adamant Workings ain't easy; the Great Contagion <i>might</i> have been one example of such that was pulled off by the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> (That said, we've been told that the Deathlords are master <i>necromancers</i>, and necromancy works differently; it may even be that they don't affect Creation, but the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-16-2015, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:17:59-08:00","id":767454,"title":"","content":"Because they don't actually want to destroy Creation.<br /> <br /> And we don't know the powers Deathlords actually have, so assuming they can do Solar workings is a flawed premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:18:51-08:00","id":767455,"title":"","content":"For one thing I don't think most of these are actually valid workings. <br /> <br /> For another, the Deathlords no longer necessarily desire the complete destruction of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:20:58-08:00","id":767458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings#post767450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals, presumably, can get at least Celestial Circle Sorcery. IIRC 2e Deathlords could have it themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Ambition 3. </b><br /> * Change a fundamental rule of the cosmos such that the air is made of lava.<br /> * Shut off Creation's reincarnation process and let things sort itself out.<br /> * Everyone that dies becomes a murderghost that murders everyone that can walk around without a shadowland.<br /> * Have the Void come alive and just eat everything Galacticus style.'<br /> * Sickness spreads like crazy and can not be cured.<br /> * All attempts at social interaction physically harm people.<br /> * Etc. Etc. Etc.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It says subtly change a metaphysical truth of the entire cosmos. Air to lava is not subtle nor metaphysical. <br /> <br /> Only one of your examples that I think might somewhat fit is the reincarnation one, and then going from working to not working at all is not subtle. They could mess with it somehow though. But there are many other ultra powerful beings to contend with in such a direct attack. Only a story could tell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:21:21-08:00","id":767459,"title":"","content":"Some possibilities...<br /> <br /> 1) Deathlords don't have access to sorcery, and necromancy doesn't work the same way.<br /> 2) Deathlords don't have access to any effects that would require XP expenditure, in a special rule that they might share with other ghosts.<br /> 3) Deathlords haven't been around for centuries in this edition. Who knows?<br /> 4) Deathlords are not motivated, either personally or by any external power, to simply kill off the world (also known as 'The End of The World is Not the Deathlord's Win Condition Anymore' theory)<br /> 5) Deathlords can only perform Creation-affecting workings in Creation, and other forces have been present to foil the attempts each time so far (hooray for Sidereals!)<br /> 6) The lack of stats beyond five keeps such workings from being a sure thing, and Deathlords are unlikely to automatically have all the needed stats at 5 just for being a Deathlord.<br /> 7) Deathlords, like most ghosts, don't have excellencies, making these workings much more difficult.<br /> <br /> Take your pick!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:27:24-08:00","id":767461,"title":"","content":"It's entirely possible that the Great Contagion was an Ambition 3 Solar Working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T17:50:12-08:00","id":767479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings#post767450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals, presumably, can get at least Celestial Circle Sorcery. IIRC 2e Deathlords could have it themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Ambition 3. </b><br /> * Change a fundamental rule of the cosmos such that the air is made of lava.<br /> * Shut off Creation's reincarnation process and let things sort itself out.<br /> * Everyone that dies becomes a Nephwrack in service to the Neverborn.<br /> * Everyone that dies becomes Chejop Kejack.<br /> * Have the Void come alive and just eat everything Galacticus style.'<br /> * Sickness spreads like crazy and can not be cured.<br /> * All attempts at social interaction physically harm people.<br /> * Etc. Etc. Etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The amount of assumptions off basically <b>no information at all</b> about the Deathlords is astounding. Who says the Deathlords are all Solars this time around, anyway?<br /> <br /> Or that they're anywhere near the same?<br /> <br /> I was always fond of the idea that the ghosts could be any sort of celestial exalted but I suspect we may never have a straight answer for them. A few? Yes, Mask of Winters is the ghost of a Solar hellbent on conquest. Nary a fuck was given that day as he conquered the hell out of Thorns. And he sits on his corpse mountain, planning who knows what.<br /> <br /> But the others are delightfully open to interpretation. A Sidereal-based Deathlord would be <b>terrifying</b>-but not necessarily planning to destroy Creation. She's working and storing her neat stuff here!<br /> <br /> Or maybe in the Underworld, there's a Mamzelle-type figure who was a Lunar shaman in life, who retired one day determined to live forever, waking to unlife in the Underworld and continuing to be a shaman and using the gris gris to get her way and form her power base. Her charms don't work, but she's still plenty smart and knows enough to make it here.<br /> <br /> And many more.<br /> <br /> (Mamzelle Marie Laveau is amazing-there's people who swear that she's still alive two hundred years later)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T18:00:05-08:00","id":767483,"title":"","content":"I think the reason this isn't the case can be summed up by a single sentence in the book: &quot;As long as the Storyteller feels that something should be possible through a sorcerous working, it can be attained through workings of the Adamant Circle.&quot;<br /> <br /> If we assume the deathlords have access to solar circle workings, and that their ultimate goal is the destruction of Creation, then the answer as to why they haven't just pulled off some workings to get it done is that such workings aren't actually possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T18:22:54-08:00","id":767495,"title":"","content":"The mechanics do not affect the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T18:27:23-08:00","id":767498,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing that SoulGambit's copy of the backer PDF had the actual details for sorcerous workings torn out and replaced with 'whatever the fuck you want to do.'<br /> <br /> Even if we assume that there's a Deathlord 1) who wants to destroy Creation, 2) is a fallen Solar, and 3) who has access to Adamant Circle Sorcery, they still wouldn't be able to do most of the stuff on your list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T18:38:25-08:00","id":767504,"title":"","content":"I'm hopeful that, due to the backlash against their 2e incarnations, the 3e Deathlords won't be &quot;Charms: Every Solar and Abyssal charm in both books&quot;, and they'll work more like demons like Octavian - a handful of scary individual panoply powers/charms, some potent combat stats, etc. As such, they won't automatically have sorcery. &quot;Okay but what about Abyssals?&quot; What about them? p179 suggests that extremely few Exalted reach Essence 4 or 5 without a century or three under their belt, and only player characters and direct rivals are apt to be those few. &quot;But what about their direct rival Abyssal?&quot; Well, isn't that what a story is for? 'Bearer of the Polysyllabic Overwrought Sobriquiet is initiating a Solar Circle Working to fuck shit up, are you a bad enough Solar dude to stop him?'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T19:00:14-08:00","id":767513,"title":"","content":"The only ones of those I would consider valid are: &quot;social interaction becomes physically painful or injurious in large quantities&quot; (at which point the majority communication in Creation becomes interpretive dance or semaphore flags) and &quot;it sucks a hell of a lot worse to be sick&quot; (what's that, life sucking for regular people? in <i>my</i> Exalted?)<br /> <br /> Like, you can't just brute-force the cosmos like that. If you declare &quot;air turns to lava&quot; that would be decidedly inconvenient until you found that everyone who used to be able to breathe air is now able to breathe lava.<br /> <br /> It still might be a little weird.<br /> <br /> I would also find it difficult to believe that the Deathlords would be written as wanting to destroy Creation and have Solar powers after constant, constant, <i>constant</i> statements by the devs and occasionally the writing staff for<i> like</i> <i>four years now</i> on why &quot;Deathlords want to destroy Creation and have Solar powers&quot; was not a thing they found desireable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T19:27:20-08:00","id":767527,"title":"","content":"I feel like this issue is solved by assuming/houseruling the following:<br /> <br /> A: Only Solars can learn Adamant Sorcery.<br /> B: Even if you attempt to go &quot;Beyond the Boundary&quot;, you cannot go higher than an Ambition 2 Working.<br /> C: Deathlords have their own unique charms, and do not have any access to their old Solar powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T19:53:08-08:00","id":767536,"title":"","content":"I thought the Deathlord's access to Solar Circle Sorcery in this edition was getting the axe. Pretty sure it was in the Dev's crosshair before even the end of 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Map of Third Edition Creation in a First Edition Style<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2F18ttip13xdsc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D35f3d332551385032587cde8b093e4923ed687ee\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b</a>, (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fpjil7fcr0esc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3Dcfdff833d8e8afe3e86ca27c06569cad0bb44be9\" target=\"_blank\">3E Locations Only</a>) (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/media?url=https%3A%2F%2Fpreview.redd.it%2Fik6dit8lrlrc1.png%3Fwidth%3D5780%26format%3Dpng%26auto%3Dwebp%26s%3D0e0c488dea6e066af00d52c6d5994592bb4d8359\" target=\"_blank\">1E, 2E, 3E Amalgam</a>)\u200b<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/kashi85\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt, where I post some Exalted stuffs.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/853-kashi","name":"Kashi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar853_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T20:13:20-08:00","id":767539,"title":"","content":"The Deathlords in 3e haven't already won by reshaping Creation via Solar level Workings the same way their 2e incarnations didn't win through application of the Creation Slaying Oblivion Kick. Because it's boring as hell to write up character sheets only to have the ST say at first session &quot;Excellent job everyone, but unfortunately 200 years ago Mask of Winters climbed Mount Meru and performed a Hook Kick to the North, a Back Kick to the East, a Scissor Kick to the South and ending with a Roundhouse Kick to the West, blasting the entirety of Creation into a lifeless wasteland. Everything then fell into the void, dragging Heaven and Hell after it. Thanks for paying for Pizza, see everyone next week?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T20:56:23-08:00","id":767553,"title":"","content":"Okay so. My /specific examples/ were a bit tongue in cheek. You would want to be smarter. &quot;The environment of creation is no longer capable of sustaining life in the long term.&quot; or make Shadowlands AMAZINGLY easy to crop up like everywhere are more what you could do. Or something else cleverrer.<br /> <br /> I am assuming Abyssals have access at least to Celestial Sorcery, which is all that is required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T21:08:47-08:00","id":767557,"title":"","content":"Maybe they don't have access to Sorcery at all. Maybe Necromantic workings only work in the Underworld or in Shadowlands. We aren't going to know how the setting is different until more books come out, until then we're just spinning out collective wheels on the old edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T21:44:50-08:00","id":767569,"title":"","content":"Hmm, actually, I think &quot;no, Abyssals DON'T get Celestial Circle Sorcery&quot; may indeed be on point;<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\">The Lunar and Sidereal Exalted may master the Terrestrial and Celestial Circles, but the final secrets of the Solar Circle elude them. Dragon-Blooded, Liminal Exalted, and mortals are only capable of initiating into the Terrestrial Circle. The Abyssal Exalted command similar raw power to their Solar counterparts, but focus on the dread secrets of necromancy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> I think that would be worded differently if Abyssals got Celestial Circle Sorcery. Interesting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T21:59:33-08:00","id":767573,"title":"","content":"Well from the looks of it the scale is kind of off. I mean a high ambition solar working can basically make a city into it's underworld counterpart or cause a city to phase in and out of existence, but it would imply that the scale it works on isn't that massive. So plunging an area into a shadowland would be a plausible thing for them, but they couldn't do it an area equal to the Blessed Isle even if they wanted to.*<br /> <br /> *Obviously I'm assuming one working here as the situation changes if we're assuming multiple workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T23:47:34-08:00","id":767612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767495#post767495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics do not affect the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more accurate to say &quot;when setting and mechanics are in conflict, it is the mechanics that are assumed in error.&quot;<br /> <br /> In response to the OP<br /> <br /> 1. Several of your examples are not plausible Solar Workings<br /> 2. We don't know whether Deathlords are capable of Solar Workings<br /> 3. Most Deathlords are not bent on Creation's destruction. Assuming all 9 that we know come back, I'd bet money that ONLY the Dowager actively seeks that goal (Bishop may, but as more long term abstraction than an imminent snuff out the light kind of thing)<br /> 4. Attempts in the past have been thwarted by heroes and Heaven. The obvious example of a thwarted plot is the Great Contagion.<br /> 4. Perhaps their Necromancy doesn't let them rewrite the Laws of Creation, but rather allows them to affect the Underworld instead. It would thematically fit the role of Abyssals as having power in Creation the Deathlords lack<br /> <br /> Now could an apocalyptically bent Abyssal Necromancer be a threat to all life... Possibly. But if so that's a problem that is only now going to start to appear as they've only existed for 5 years. Better get some PCs on the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-17-2015, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T01:58:47-08:00","id":767665,"title":"","content":"I'd say that when the question of subtly modifying creation's laws is thought of, it should be defined as &quot;this cna't simply lolnope the current laws or their intent.&quot; You can't make creation antethetical to life, because part of its purpose is to support life. <br /> Also, note that ambition 3 solar workings are very difficult, <i>even for experienced solars</i> and probably set off all sorts of alarms on the loom. A deathlord who does this, whether he fails or succeeds just shot to the top of everyones &quot;to do&quot; list and that might include the Unconquered Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T03:44:26-08:00","id":767722,"title":"","content":"Also, Abyssals have only been around for a few years. They won't have destroyed Creation 100 years ago because they only started existing, what, 5 years ago? Maybe only a handful have advanced to the necromantic equivalent of the Celestial Circle, and none have advanced to the Void Circle yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T03:53:48-08:00","id":767725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767553#post767553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so. My /specific examples/ were a bit tongue in cheek. You would want to be smarter. &quot;The environment of creation is no longer capable of sustaining life in the long term.&quot; or make Shadowlands AMAZINGLY easy to crop up like everywhere are more what you could do. Or something else cleverrer.<br /> <br /> I am assuming Abyssals have access at least to Celestial Sorcery, which is all that is required.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only things suggested to be Creation wide are subtle changes to metaphysical truths. Also they theres opposition. The gods serve some purpose. Its not just Sorcery and whatever it will affect in a vacuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T04:07:54-08:00","id":767727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767527#post767527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this issue is solved by assuming/houseruling the following:</div> </div> </div> </div>There's really no issue ITT at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:30:54-08:00","id":767761,"title":"","content":"I always thought the Abyssal/Deathlord plot was the make creation into a big enough shadowland that their masters could escape, or drag creation into the underworld so that their masters could use it to get to heaven and revive themselves. You know, not actually about mindlessly destroying creation but surgically doing so. This may have been part of the reason The Lion was punished by welding his armor to his body. They wanted him to suffer for nearly destroying the goal, and preventing their escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:34:24-08:00","id":767762,"title":"","content":"The Neverborn are dreaming, insane and dead. Who can say for sure what their goals are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:35:44-08:00","id":767764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767761#post767761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the Abyssal/Deathlord plot was the make creation into a big enough shadowland that their masters could escape, or drag creation into the underworld so that their masters could use it to get to heaven and revive themselves. You know, not actually about mindlessly destroying creation but surgically doing so. This may have been part of the reason The Lion was punished by welding his armor to his body. They wanted him to suffer for nearly destroying the goal, and preventing their escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the point was to pull Creation into Oblivion so that maybe when it was gone the Neverborn could get sucked in too. I forget if it was canon or fanon that Creation was basically one giant Fetter for the Neverborn and while they could never pass through Lethe it still prevented them from moving on in some other way <br /> <br /> What you proposed sounds neat but also sounds a little too close to the 2e Reclamation for my liking. The Neverborn have never been described with that level of personal agency that they could go anywhere let alone revive themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:36:44-08:00","id":767765,"title":"","content":"It was also sort of what Eye and Seven Despairs believed in (destroy Creation, let the Neverborn get sucked into the Wyld where there is no causality anymore, instant resurrection).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T05:39:28-08:00","id":767767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767612#post767612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's more accurate to say &quot;when setting and mechanics are in conflict, it is the mechanics that are assumed in error.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that they're in error so much as one needs to understand what their priority is.<br /> <br /> Rules for high level sorcerous workings are calibrated as a way for players to achieve such things, possibly with some major obstacles, but otherwise reasonably enough that they would actually pursue and acquire it. This facilitates players engaging with the setting in terms of grand, storied heroes. People in the setting are not making assumptions about the capacity for workings that players will get from the rules, and even if it still winds up as something within relative reach, most are probably not pursuing it so earnestly.<br /> <br /> I mean, even with regards to whether or not a Deathlord would want such a thing... I would still assume that there are some Deathlords who want to kill the world, for some meaning of that term, and have been earnestly pursuing it, and while the mechanics for something like sorcery might reflect the internal difficulties, they don't quite map to it. Which is to say that even if somebody has tried in those circumstances where they've managed to not be distracted or interrupted, something has been a bit beyond them.<br /> <br /> Regarding transferring the action to Abyssals (or possibly any other being who can wield sorcery), I feel as though the rules are meant to reflect a subtle setting reality in which getting somebody else to perform a working on your behalf doesn't quite work, given that sidebar about summoning demon sorcerers.<br /> <br /> In any case... yeah, one needs to recognise the edges beyond which the rules aren't really covering the setting.<br /> <br /> I take a similar attitude to battle groups; they're good for presenting small groups of great warriors fighting powerful forces, and a form of battle command that is reasonably low-key to be reconciled with a system to represent the dramatic interactions between powerful individuals, but I don't think you could really represent battles between tens or hundreds of thousands of individuals with it (at least not in a form that wouldn't kind of drain the drama out of it). Yet, such armies exist in the setting, and I would say they're operating at a scale at which an Exalt who could handily fight a couple thousand* will think in terms of the need for another army in response.<br /> <br /> * I also think that this is a thing that people in the setting will treat as harder and more dangerous (and thus impressive for those who manage it) than the rules strictly represent, even if the rules make a decent challenge of it. Hell, I think this about matters involving less than a hundred of some well known elite troops, such as Brides of Ahlat or Gem's Market Guard (even if those could probably rock some fairly good dice pools and defences, especially if they've got a decent commander).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T06:46:50-08:00","id":767790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767765#post767765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was also sort of what Eye and Seven Despairs believed in (destroy Creation, let the Neverborn get sucked into the Wyld where there is no causality anymore, instant resurrection).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but Eye and Seven spent nearly all his time finding ways to hunt down and screw over a specific handful of people. He's the poster child for how ineffective the Neverborn's minions are because they all pay lip service to the whole 'destroy everything ever' goal, but pretty much none of them actually want to succeed.<br /> <br /> The way they behave in canon fiction and the way most people NPC them, the Deathlord's version of the Great Curse is Villainous Attention Deficit Disorder. &quot;Yessss, my power will blanket Creation in eternal ni... hey, that guy was a dick to me in my past life! Ravening hordes of unstoppable corpse-warriors, after him! I'm gonna lock him in a box and read terrible poetry at him for a thousand years!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T07:23:30-08:00","id":767810,"title":"","content":"I just got an idea for sid story &quot;Return of the TeaCup Ninjas: Sabotage of Dreaded Workings&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T08:55:28-08:00","id":767847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767762#post767762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Neverborn are dreaming, insane and dead. Who can say for sure what their goals are?</div> </div> </div> </div>...so, can they read a letter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:00:03-08:00","id":767853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767847#post767847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...so, can they read a letter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Will this become a new meme ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:08:04-08:00","id":767857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767847#post767847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...so, can they read a letter?</div> </div> </div> </div>They have no eyes, so probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:21:28-08:00","id":767864,"title":"","content":"Deathlord Linguistics charm specifically for reading the Neverborn's mail to them from a safe distance: confirmed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T09:26:15-08:00","id":767871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767847#post767847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...so, can they read a letter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well played.<br /> <br /> ... although, given what happened the <i>first</i> time someone killed them, do we really want to know what'll happen the second time? The creation of Industrial Strength Death and the Undererworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T10:50:35-08:00","id":767949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767871#post767871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well played.<br /> <br /> ... although, given what happened the <i>first</i> time someone killed them, do we really want to know what'll happen the second time? The creation of Industrial Strength Death and the Undererworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would actually kill them as such. Rather, it would make them enter lethe, ie, the cycle of reincarnation. So... whatever happens, it's likely to be world-shattering and terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T11:52:09-08:00","id":767981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767949#post767949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it would actually kill them as such. Rather, it would make them enter lethe, ie, the cycle of reincarnation. So... whatever happens, it's likely to be world-shattering and terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather doubt this charm can make them enter Lethe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T12:35:45-08:00","id":768020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767981#post767981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather doubt this charm can make them enter Lethe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Cup Boils Over does. I'd agree that it probably doesn't work on the Neverborn at all, but if it does affect them in any way, it sends them off to lethe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T16:16:03-08:00","id":768156,"title":"","content":"To do a working affecting a road, you have to do rituals and mystic stuff along that road. To do a working affecting all of Creation\u2026 you may not have to go to every last part of it, but you'd need to be doing big ritual effects in places all over Creation. And something on that level is going to get noticed, by the gods whose purviews are being affected, by the Sidereals as it resonates through the Loom of Fate, and others. Especially given it's a difficulty 2 IntOcc roll for a Sorcerer to notice 'the encroaching effects of a working on a region'. And the region for this is the whole world. <br /> <br /> If you're Salina, and you have the backing (or at least acceptance) of the other Exalts of your time, and can go all across the Creation to do your rituals, then yes, you can write the ability to learn sorcery into the very world itself.<br /> <br /> If you're a bunch of PCs who want to cripple the Guild by using a working to taint the nature of silver (one of their nightmares and why they still hold onto a fair bit of Jade), then it's going to be damn hard, but doing rituals along the Guild trade routes, and at hordes of silver, then yeah, you might be able to do it. It'll be damn hard, you'll want distractions to keep the Guild busy (as mortals they're likely at least somewhat less understanding of workings), and work out how you stop the Sidereals, Lunars, and Realm interfering. But it could be possible, because it's &quot;Change the world and hurt the Guild&quot; not &quot;Destroy the world&quot; <br /> Specific, targeted workings may well be a weapon the Deathlords and their minions use. But it's not going to be a &quot;I sit at home, I make some rolls, the world is fucked.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/30-fearmeforiampink","name":"FearMeForIAmPink","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar30_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T17:22:53-08:00","id":768186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768020#post768020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what Cup Boils Over does. I'd agree that it probably doesn't work on the Neverborn at all, but if it does affect them in any way, it sends them off to lethe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I meant I doubt it affects them at all, in part because I don't think their Intimacies would qualify, and because I doubt something that never built Lethe to work on it could enter Lethe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T17:24:30-08:00","id":768187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767727#post767727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's really no issue ITT at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the examples given are somewhat exaggerated, I'd argue that there is still a problem if the Deathlords have access to Celestial Sorcery.<br /> <br /> While turning the air in to lava isn't exactly a subtle alteration of reality, performing a Working that damages the integrity of Creation so it's actively being absorbed by Shadowlands is within the scope of an Ambition 3 Solar working. While the rate of Creation's decay is unlikely to be fast enough that it falls in to Perma-Shadowland next week, a Deathlord who wants to doom Creation (not destroy, just doom) can put it in to a more or less irreversible death spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 11-17-2015, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T18:17:51-08:00","id":768214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768187#post768187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the examples given are somewhat exaggerated, I'd argue that there is still a problem if the Deathlords have access to Celestial Sorcery.<br /> <br /> While turning the air in to lava isn't exactly a subtle alteration of reality, performing a Working that damages the integrity of Creation it's actively being absorbed by Shadowlands is within the scope of an Ambition 3 Solar working. While the rate of Creation's decay is unlikely to be fast enough that it falls in to Perma-Shadowland next week, a Deathlord who wants to doom Creation (not destroy, just doom) can put it in to a more or less irreversible death spiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a Working can be undone with another Working, right? Something of that scale, the Lunars and Sidereals would notice eventually, and I'm willing to bet that there are more Celestial Sorcerers among the 100 Sidereals and aproximately 400 Lunars than among the 13 Deathlords.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T18:45:57-08:00","id":768224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768214#post768214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Working can be undone with another Working, right? Something of that scale, the Lunars and Sidereals would notice eventually, and I'm willing to bet that there are more Celestial Sorcerers among the 100 Sidereals and aproximately 400 Lunars than among the 13 Deathlords.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this hypothetical it depends on the rate of decay. Too slow, and the Shadowlanding of Creation might be so gradual and the Sids and Lunars will be too busy fighting each other that it will go unnoticed until it's too late. Too fast, and by the time you get you counter-working in place (which will take months) vast swaths of Creation will be Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Plus on a side note, it also raises the question of why Sidereals and Lunars aren't using their Celestial to Solar Workings to make Creation more antagonistic for each other.<br /> <br /> Honestly I feel like most of these issues go away if you limit the Beyond the Boundary effects to Ambition 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T18:47:08-08:00","id":768225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768214#post768214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a Working can be undone with another Working, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually undone? No. Effectively nullified while still being fully in effect by means of another working of opposed effect? Yes.<br /> <br /> Subtle, but important difference.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T14:23:14-08:00","id":768721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768225#post768225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually undone? No. Effectively nullified while still being fully in effect by means of another working of opposed effect? Yes.<br /> <br /> Subtle, but important difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in other words, if we pretend &quot;turn air to lava&quot; is a valid working, you could counter it with a working making everyone immune to the heat of lava, and being able to breathe it. The air would still be lava though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9008-staffan","name":"Staffan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T14:26:55-08:00","id":768724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767847#post767847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...so, can they read a letter?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>KILLBRUSH CUPBOILER, CHOSEN OF THE SUN: </b>Yo dogg, your existence is pointless. You should let your soul fall into Lethe and just peace on the whole apocalypse thing.<br /> <br /> <b>NON-CANONICALLY LUCID NEVERBORN: </b>but I already TRIED that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T15:46:57-08:00","id":768757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Staffan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768721#post768721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in other words, if we pretend &quot;turn air to lava&quot; is a valid working, you could counter it with a working making everyone immune to the heat of lava, and being able to breathe it. The air would still be lava though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they just changed the &quot;Air is Lava&quot; into a metaphysical thought where the lava-air is perfectly breathable and natural, but as a cruel consequence the natural floor would then be painful to the touch in this metaphysical dream state. Of course, this metaphysical aspect of creation would only appear to the most attuned minds of dreams--the children, who could not understand how lava-air would be nice and wood-floor would be painful, immediately reversing it in their minds so that, in fact, they get terrified of the floor, but turn it into a game.<br /> <br /> And thus the Deathlord's attempts to destroy Creation turned into a child's game of &quot;The floor is lava.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T15:52:29-08:00","id":768761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768757#post768757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they just changed the &quot;Air is Lava&quot; into a metaphysical thought where the lava-air is perfectly breathable and natural, but as a cruel consequence the natural floor would then be painful to the touch in this metaphysical dream state. Of course, this metaphysical aspect of creation would only appear to the most attuned minds of dreams--the children, who could not understand how lava-air would be nice and wood-floor would be painful, immediately reversing it in their minds so that, in fact, they get terrified of the floor, but turn it into a game.<br /> <br /> And thus the Deathlord's attempts to destroy Creation turned into a child's game of &quot;The floor is lava.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just for kids any more.<br /> <br /> (somewhat NSFW)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/J25H5qk.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"color:#696969\">When all the world was very young<br /> And mountain magic heavy hung<br /> The supermen would walk in file<br /> Guardians of a loveless isle</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2010-root","name":"Root","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1014"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T16:56:11-08:00","id":768794,"title":"","content":"It has always been my read that the Neverborn are inverted principals of the universe that while inconvenient in comparison to what they were, are so fundamental to existence that completing their annihilation would, in general, destroy all of Creation, on a quantum level. So, ultimate victory for them, while simple in concept, is ultimately beyond even a Primordial's ability. You might swing it with the aid of a few Shinma, but finding, entreating, and convincing them to aid you to such an end just isn't going to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T18:30:56-08:00","id":768826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768724#post768724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>KILLBRUSH CUPBOILER, CHOSEN OF THE SUN: </b>Yo dogg, your existence is pointless. You should let your soul fall into Lethe and just peace on the whole apocalypse thing.<br /> <br /> <b>NON-CANONICALLY LUCID NEVERBORN: </b>but I already TRIED that!</div> </div> </div> </div>it feels like something fundementally wrong addressing a neverborn with the phrase &quot;yo dogg&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8919-kitmehsu","name":"kitmehsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8919_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:27:42-08:00","id":768939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768225#post768225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually undone? No. Effectively nullified while still being fully in effect by means of another working of opposed effect? Yes.<br /> <br /> Subtle, but important difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you could explicitly use a Working to actually undo another Working/Spell, not just negate it with an opposite effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:48:10-08:00","id":768953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768939#post768939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought you could explicitly use a Working to actually undo another Working/Spell, not just negate it with an opposite effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope you can't distort or undo a working once one has been made. The book explicitly says that the closest one can come is to perform a working that counters the effects of the first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:03:29-08:00","id":768962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kitmehsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768826#post768826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it feels like something fundementally wrong addressing a neverborn with the phrase &quot;yo dogg&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hwaet! Ye doge,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:07:01-08:00","id":768963,"title":"","content":"Frankly, if it's only their access to Celestial Circle Sorcery that matters, one should probably ask why the <i>Lunars</i> haven't &quot;won&quot; yet. Their Celestial sorcerers probably outnumber Deathlords about 3 to 1, and are actually in the world they want to affect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:24:18-08:00","id":768971,"title":"","content":"... That is true. AND Dragonblooded don't have Terrestrial Sorcery. Lunars could just Solar 3 working to make Dragonblooded suck more. Then again, maybe they already did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:54:06-08:00","id":768980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768971#post768971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... That is true. AND Dragonblooded don't have Terrestrial Sorcery. Lunars could just Solar 3 working to make Dragonblooded suck more. Then again, maybe they already did.</div> </div> </div> </div>It bounced off and hit the first two editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:03:40-08:00","id":768985,"title":"","content":"Rakshi can't just take a 300 year break to craft a Solar Working that snipes from her workroom across creation to make the blessed isle suffer famine and woe for a thousand years. If she wanted to do something like that, she'd have to perform it on the blessed isle. I'm fairly certain that someone would notice and a hundred dragon blooded would swarm her. If she didn't die, then at the very least her working would be disrupted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:56:41-08:00","id":769007,"title":"","content":"I think there's something important to note about sorcerous workings.<br /> <br /> I don't think that sorcerers literally have the power to do anything, any way, (other than true resurrection and time travel) if they roll enough dice.<br /> I think there are many sorcerous rituals that are possible, enough that, for the sake of fun and not writing an entire book detailing them, the ST is given a relatively free-form system for assigning rules and difficulties to them. In reality, each of these rituals requires various ingredients and processes that are hand-waved to be stunted by the player.<br /> <br /> For example, maybe to summon the demon Nakak-Shadar, the Blight Between Worlds, you have to do the ritual on the 3rd day of an inauspicious week, and sacrifice an albino creature with a bronze knife which was previously used to kill an innocent, but the rules don't go into this much detail, because it's easier for the player to just describe it however he wanted.<br /> <br /> As another example, my No Moon wanted to get rid of his Lunar tattoos. So, he went to the Wyld with his Fair Folk buddy, and spent a long time ingesting as much wyld-tainted fruit as he could, and spent time meditating underwater in the wyldzone's river. Then, on the night of the New Moon, he used Flesh-Crafting Art to rearrange his tattooed skin so it was all on his arms and legs, and had the Fair Folk cut them off (leaving him with no skin, limbs, or tattoos). This weakened his tattoos enough that by focusing his mutagenic power, he burst them off him.<br /> Then he used his charms to regrow his limbs and skin and went to say a guy with Order-Conferring Blow so he could get rid of his 5 pre-tattooing mutations (which were impossible to get off while he was tattooed).<br /> And unfortunately he botched a roll, so he discovered his shadow had run off to become a creepy perverted monster that spies on his daughter in bed with her husband. Now he has no shadow (except when it sneaks back and hides behind him, mocking him with rude gestures).<br /> <br /> Now, RAW, I didn't have to do all that stuff: I just had to roll the dice. But, fluff-wise, that is how he did it, he didn't just roll cosmic dice. With his Intelligence and Occult, he worked out how to do a ritual that would get rid of his tattoos. And what he then did, was what he had to do; if he hadn't eaten all that wyld-fruit, it wouldn't have worked. If he didn't botch one of the rolls, he would have realised he had made a mistake in his ritual, and done something else, so that his shadow didn't run off and become a pervy monster.<br /> The rules are just a free-form system for using the variety of rituals, they're not saying &quot;any sorcerer can do any kind of magic any way he likes at any time, if he takes a few weeks and knows tons about Occult&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, it might well be that the Deathlords can't do a ritual to make air poisonous to humans, because the rules don't let them do literally everything.<br /> Fluff-wise, they can make the air poisonous to humans by building 5 mighty soulsteel towers, one at each pole, which if fed the heart of a Solar on the last night of Calibration while the Deathlord sings paens to the Neverborn, will make air poisonous to humans.<br /> Or they could stop humans reincarnating by building a giant bone engine on the site of the Heavenly ministry of souls and feeding Saturn and all her children into its maw to power it.<br /> It's just that, these things aren't practical.<br /> On the other hand, they might try doing such a thing in future, and when they do, various forces (like the PCs) will find out about it and have to go on a quest to stop it!<br /> <br /> Previously, the Dowager did do a mighty working: she spent years (to get enough means) to search the Well of Udr for a plague to unleash on humanity with incredible contagion-power and a huge mortality rate (Finesse 5). Eventually, she found it and unleashed it, but it was stopped by the Fair Folk invasion (because even at Finesse 5, the player doesn't choose 100% of the effects).<br /> Since then, she's been spending years looking for a similar plague to unleash, but hasn't found it yet (she hasn't rolled well enough, and to get enough means she only rolls once a year or something).<br /> But maybe one day she'll find a new plague (by getting a lucky roll on her Int+Occult) and unleash it on Creation again!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T00:09:20-08:00","id":769011,"title":"","content":"Also, if the Mask of Winters could have just made a ritual to make Thorns Fall to him, he would never have had to starve the city by laying siege to it, then sending in pigs and cattle tainted with Puppeteers' Plague for the starving people to eat that made their skeletons rip from their flesh and murder people. I know exactly which option is more flavorful and it's not &quot;A wizard did it&quot; despite the fact that it was a wizard who done it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T01:18:56-08:00","id":769036,"title":"","content":"This might not be entirely popular, but I feel like Sorcerous Workings shouldn't just be &quot;wave your arms in the air for a few weeks&quot; either. Like if you want to stick wings on a trex you're gonna need to start with something with wings (or at least that looks kinda like wings) and a trex. If you want to change the laws of Creation, you're probably going to be travelling to the elemental poles to weave your spell into them. I love Workings and what they can achieve, but I don't feel they should replace roleplay with literal IC handwaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T01:56:46-08:00","id":769046,"title":"","content":"I agree, and I don't think they're supposed to replace roleplaying (see my post at the end of the last page).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T02:19:54-08:00","id":769054,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing where the belief that one can't &quot;just wave their arms for a few weeks&quot; to do a working would be unpopular. Afterall the three traits that make up a working are ambition, finesse, and means. I mean finesse is just the how this working will alter the world specifically to accomplish the ambition. Means is literally resources, skills, allies, anything you can put toward the task beyond just being a sorcerer. Heck the means paragraph actually mentions that it is intended that you'll need additional means in order to accomplish more ambitious workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:27:02-08:00","id":769224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768953#post768953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope you can't distort or undo a working once one has been made. The book explicitly says that the closest one can come is to perform a working that counters the effects of the first.</div> </div> </div> </div>A working that puts a whole satrapy to sleep is going to be reversed by someone using a working that makes them sleep and wake normally regardless of whether you consider the original working to be 'undone', the only difference is that you can't specifically use the counterspell or spell distortion rules on it. (Which I'm pretty sure was what the author meant by that section.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:14:03-08:00","id":769365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769224#post769224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A working that puts a whole satrapy to sleep is going to be reversed by someone using a working that makes them sleep and wake normally regardless of whether you consider the original working to be 'undone', the only difference is that you can't specifically use the counterspell or spell distortion rules on it. (Which I'm pretty sure was what the author meant by that section.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. I mean yeah they can be countered in the effect of not really having an impact on the world anymore, but the example in that section pretty much implies both effects are still in play they just don't amount to anything in the grand scheme. That's why the example in the section has a road that has a working on it to speed and slow travel on it ends with a merchant who has a really weird story about the journey. For those who haven't read the section basically the part that speeds traffic causes elementals and spirits of the area to aid the travelers of the road to make the journey faster. The slow part causes the horse to refuse to go on the road and the entire thing makes the traveler exceptionally cautious. End result the elementals and spirits handled cargo transport and calming the traveler but as they have to do all that as well the trip takes no longer than it would have had neither effect been in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:19:40-08:00","id":769372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769224#post769224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A working that puts a whole satrapy to sleep is going to be reversed by someone using a working that makes them sleep and wake normally regardless of whether you consider the original working to be 'undone', the only difference is that you can't specifically use the counterspell or spell distortion rules on it. (Which I'm pretty sure was what the author meant by that section.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it might be undone by a working that lets them act whilst asleep. Or one that lets them manifest dream-selves that go around and do stuff in the area around their body, whilst their body sleeps. Or many other weird and wonderful ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/30-fearmeforiampink","name":"FearMeForIAmPink","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar30_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:24:48-08:00","id":769425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769224#post769224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A working that puts a whole satrapy to sleep is going to be reversed by someone using a working that makes them sleep and wake normally regardless of whether you consider the original working to be 'undone', the only difference is that you can't specifically use the counterspell or spell distortion rules on it. (Which I'm pretty sure was what the author meant by that section.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, let's take &quot;put a whole satrapy to sleep.&quot; I'm the Dowager, and I tell my Storyteller I'm going to do that, Solar Circle working, everything goes as planned. Finesse 5 means I pretty much have full control in designing the working, and then let the Storyteller do the dev work to make sure it balances out. So, what's the duration of the curse? I'm not going to submit a sleep plague that lasts forever indefinitely and unconditionally, because any ST can have the sense to shoot that down. A year and a day? Until a queen's blood is spilled? More likely to get a yes. Other common sense questions, like &quot;can I just stab a sleeping dude?&quot; are probably going to come up at some point, and at that point I need to answer them. There are limits keeping me from omnipotence in obtaining my goals through the working, but they're largely limits that I get to pick. <br /> <br /> Once a sorcerous working is done, it's done. When one sorcerer tries to tear down another's working, the intent at the heart of the counter-working is not &quot;undo that,&quot; but a positive or constructive sorcerous accomplishment that negates its effect on the world around it. When you roll into the Sleeping Satrapy, you can't wake everyone up as a working. If you want to fix things, you'd need to engage with either the effects of the working (&quot;I tear down the veil between waking and dreaming, and everything goes back to being mostly normal except for being a gestalt shared reality&quot;) or its limitations (&quot;It's just going to rain queens until there's enough blood, damn it!&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T12:03:21-08:00","id":769445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769425#post769425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, let's take &quot;put a whole satrapy to sleep.&quot; I'm the Dowager, and I tell my Storyteller I'm going to do that, Solar Circle working, everything goes as planned. </div> </div> </div> </div>Completely unimportant but is a curse of sleep Solar level? isnt terrestial enough?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T12:05:37-08:00","id":769449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769445#post769445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Completely unimportant but is a curse of sleep Solar level? isnt terrestial enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>An entire satrapy is a bigger chunk of geographic area than Terrestrial workings can generally handle, even though Ambition 3 is hyperbole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T12:08:58-08:00","id":769451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769445#post769445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Completely unimportant but is a curse of sleep Solar level? isnt terrestial enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>ambition 3 terrestrial curse is &quot;Place a curse on a small region in a way that diminishes, warps, or blights its mundane aspects such as flora, fauna, or natural resources, making it all but impossible to make a livelihood off the cursed land.&quot; while an Ambition 2 Solar working can &quot;Lay a potent curse on a city, region, or group of people that can only be broken when specific circumstances are met.&quot;. I'd say pulling a sleeping beauty-style curse would fall intro the second example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T16:24:07-08:00","id":769616,"title":"","content":"....And now I'm thinking of all those spells in Disney's Gargoyles that all have these clauses at the end, that simply sound like poetic terms for 'never' but are actually hard coded ending conditions for the spell. The two examples I can think of offhand were one that turned a group of people to stone until &quot;The Castle rose above the Clouds&quot; and another that turned anyone who saw and heard the spell being worked to stone during the night, until &quot;the sky burns.&quot;<br /> <br /> In the first case, the mega rich guy bought the castle, had it disassembled and rebuilt on top of his New York skyscraper which was, yes, tall enough to be above the cloud line. The second one they sprayed a flammable compound into the upper atmosphere and lit it.<br /> <br /> Nothing required magic, just science and money.<br /> <br /> Another spell caused the person it was used on to obey the person holding the spell. They solved that one by commanding the person to act normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T17:06:24-08:00","id":769648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=768224#post768224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this hypothetical it depends on the rate of decay. Too slow, and the Shadowlanding of Creation might be so gradual and the Sids and Lunars will be too busy fighting each other that it will go unnoticed until it's too late. Too fast, and by the time you get you counter-working in place (which will take months) vast swaths of Creation will be Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Plus on a side note, it also raises the question of why Sidereals and Lunars aren't using their Celestial to Solar Workings to make Creation more antagonistic for each other.<br /> <br /> Honestly I feel like most of these issues go away if you limit the Beyond the Boundary effects to Ambition 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Altering Creation is not consequence free. And if you fuck up something affecting <i>all of Creation,</i> those are some <i>nasty</i> consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T17:16:35-08:00","id":769658,"title":"","content":"But seriously though. Lunars banding together to get someone to do a Solar 2 working to curse the blessed isle feels like a much more productive use of time than &quot;send wave after wave of barbarians at their satrapies.&quot; <br /> <br /> Then again, maybe the Silver Pact is ruled by that most ancient and majestic of Lunars, Zapp Brannigan and his invisible Fair Folk ally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T17:38:32-08:00","id":769668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769658#post769658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But seriously though. Lunars banding together to get someone to do a Solar 2 working to curse the blessed isle feels like a much more productive use of time than &quot;send wave after wave of barbarians at their satrapies.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe the Silver Pact is ruled by that most ancient and majestic of Lunars, Zapp Brannigan and his invisible Fair Folk ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd probably get the parties attempting it to go up in a gout of green fire, just like how the Seven Tigers thought that they could move on the Empress just after she secured the Imperial Manse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T17:46:46-08:00","id":769675,"title":"","content":"maybe the Lunars want to dismantle the Realm, not permanently blight and salt about a 1/5th of Creation's landmass so no one can live there once the Realm is dismantled. This isn't a game of Civilization where you can just wipe a side from the board if you're the only side with nukes and then let the broken and irradiated remains of their land lie abandoned and unused while you coast on to a science win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9258-col","name":"CoL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T18:54:12-08:00","id":769711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769449#post769449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An entire satrapy is a bigger chunk of geographic area than Terrestrial workings can generally handle, even though Ambition 3 is hyperbole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so its about scale not effect. Gona have to remember that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T19:21:47-08:00","id":769721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769711#post769711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, so its about scale not effect. Gona have to remember that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I imagine its a bit of mix of the two. On the one hand yeah it would obviously be an easier working to put a specific individual to sleep for a year and a day than it would an entire satrapy. On the otherhand making the hyperbolic time chamber that's being discussed in a different thread is unlikely to not be a high level working even if your objective is just an area the size of a broom closet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T19:30:34-08:00","id":769725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769711#post769711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, so its about scale not effect. Gona have to remember that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its a bit of both. When you read the Ambition section it says that it is about power and scope. It then scales by Circle. You then balance out the area you want to cover with the extent of the change you want to cause. It mentions, for example, that Terrestrial Circle Workings should deal with the natural world somehow, not with &quot;supernatural&quot; stuff (its a bit weird on that part), it then goes on to say that if you want to do the most radical change allowed by this Circle it would be restricted to a chamber of a structure, or one single being.<br /> <br /> Lets say you want to change people into \u00dcbermensch.<br /> <br /> With Terrestrial Circle you can change one person<br /> <br /> With Celestial Circle you can change an entire village, or a neighborhood of a city and they can fly.<br /> <br /> With Solar Circle you can change the the whole country and besides flying they can shoot laser from their eyes.<br /> <br /> (Something like that, didn't really consider specifics)<br /> <br /> Its a balance act. The less drastic the effect the more area it affects. And then the values just escalate upwards as you ascend the Circles.<br /> <br /> Like you can bless a village and its surroundings to have bountiful crops at the Terrestrial Circle. You can probably do a whole Direction with Solar Circle, if that is all that you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 11-19-2015, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T05:31:22-08:00","id":769887,"title":"","content":"Thats what i meant, its about scale that is it a solar working even though the effect is terrestial. So a simple working with a bigger area of effect may need a higher circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:17:10-08:00","id":769916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings#post767450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssals, presumably, can get at least Celestial Circle Sorcery. IIRC 2e Deathlords could have it themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Ambition 3. </b><br /> * Change a fundamental rule of the cosmos such that the air is made of lava.<br /> * Shut off Creation's reincarnation process and let things sort itself out.<br /> * Everyone that dies becomes a Nephwrack in service to the Neverborn.<br /> * Everyone that dies becomes Chejop Kejack.<br /> * Have the Void come alive and just eat everything Galacticus style.'<br /> * Sickness spreads like crazy and can not be cured.<br /> * All attempts at social interaction physically harm people.<br /> * Etc. Etc. Etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like your silly, tongue in cheek examples are so far beyond the realm of reasonable workings that I can't take your argument seriously. So . . . Good job I guess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:29:15-08:00","id":769923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769887#post769887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats what i meant, its about scale that is it a solar working even though the effect is terrestial. So a simple working with a bigger area of effect may need a higher circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah cool, its just that you said &quot;scale not effect&quot; when maybe you meant &quot;scale and effect&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:34:42-08:00","id":769930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769923#post769923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah cool, its just that you said &quot;scale not effect&quot; when maybe you meant &quot;scale and effect&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was the scale not the effect <i>that made the working solar level.</i> Saving words to protect the environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T06:57:17-08:00","id":769950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=769658#post769658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But seriously though. Lunars banding together to get someone to do a Solar 2 working to curse the blessed isle feels like a much more productive use of time than &quot;send wave after wave of barbarians at their satrapies.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to recheck the rules to see how close you need to be to the thing you're trying to affect, even considering the point that a single working having overt effects on a continental landmass is out of sorts.<br /> <br /> The idea of certain Lunars strategically and surgically doing that kind of thing is probably valid, but kind of the whole point is that you don't have free ride over an empire run by thousands of hostile Exalted.<br /> <br /> Likewise, it would be pretty darn terrible if workings just turned into the new form of cruise missiles that somebody could just sit in their fortress building and lobbing out across the entire setting.<br /> <br /> I'd say that's really a basic answer to the original question; because the setting is not intended to be something over which sorcerers run roughshod, and to whatever hopefully minor extent that the rules for workings could be extended into being able to do so, the Orichalcum Rule applies.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is great, but I feel as though, at the very least, there's a point at which trying to use it to do every little thing means you're distracted from the cabal of kung-fu masters who come up to punch your heart out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T08:18:43-08:00","id":770009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767504#post767504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hopeful that, due to the backlash against their 2e incarnations, the 3e Deathlords won't be &quot;Charms: Every Solar and Abyssal charm in both books&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, always felt like people overblew out of proportion what was mostly a quick/lazy 3 word blurb/patch in the 2e corebook. Ah, yeah, you probably mean the even lazier/bothersome resume for the Bodhisattva's charmset in CoCD: Underworld. That was amazingly sloppy - not to mention the bunch of gratuitous stat hints about him being Desus, that made no godamn sense whatsoever, but i digress.<br /> <br /> Redacted it to &quot;<b>Any</b> Abyssal Charms with the Mirror Keyword and Solar Charms, whose themes don't run counter to abyssal/neverborn ones, for which he possesses the prerequisite Ability ratings&quot; without blinking and nary a care everafter. Sometimes i feel like the forums with its vitriol heap far too much attention on bits like these than they ever merited.<br /> <br /> On the main topic, whatever else the Deathlords might or not be able to do - and i bet there will be much pulling of hair &amp; gnashing of teeth anyway when this definition does come up - i would say a major complication in their plans is just how antagonistic &amp; conspirational against each other they can be and have always been in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-21-2015, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:23:02-08:00","id":770196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=770009#post770009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">retarded</div> </div> </div> </div>Friendly mod warning that there's better words with less baggage than this one.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T12:55:44-08:00","id":770226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=767790#post767790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, but Eye and Seven spent nearly all his time finding ways to hunt down and screw over a specific handful of people. He's the poster child for how ineffective the Neverborn's minions are because they all pay lip service to the whole 'destroy everything ever' goal, but pretty much none of them actually want to succeed.<br /> <br /> The way they behave in canon fiction and the way most people NPC them, the Deathlord's version of the Great Curse is Villainous Attention Deficit Disorder. &amp;quot;Yessss, my power will blanket Creation in eternal ni... hey, that guy was a dick to me in my past life! Ravening hordes of unstoppable corpse-warriors, after him! I'm gonna lock him in a box and read terrible poetry at him for a thousand years!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's important to remember that part of the reason for this is that in the end they are just ghosts, echoes of the strongest passions of their past selves. They are hideously powerful, but they are flat characters ultimately-- existing literally only through their ties to what they once were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T13:09:53-08:00","id":770236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=770226#post770226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's important to remember that part of the reason for this is that in the end they are just ghosts, echoes of the strongest passions of their past selves. They are hideously powerful, but they are flat characters ultimately-- existing literally only through their ties to what they once were.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, and Eye and Seven was pretty screwed up and obsessive even when he was alive IIRC. I wasn't criticising the Deathlords as a story feature, just pointing out that purely from a viewpoint of whether they're an effective minion/apocalyptgineer, they really suck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T13:17:30-08:00","id":770240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=770236#post770236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true, and Eye and Seven was pretty screwed up and obsessive even when he was alive IIRC. I wasn't criticising the Deathlords as a story feature, just pointing out that purely from a viewpoint of whether they're an effective minion/apocalyptgineer, they really suck.</div> </div> </div> </div> can't Argue with that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:31:21-08:00","id":770294,"title":"","content":"This is the kind of thing where I really want the Deathlords (and other major figures in the setting) to be written as being forces that can be complex and multifaceted enough that they have effects radiating out into the world without them having direct power operating at that scope, at the same time as they engage in personal details. The Sovereign of Chains can be the Timeless Order of Manacle and Coin at the same time as he's obsessed over meeting his wife again. surely Eye and Seven Despairs can be an iconic representation of death at the same time as he plays sick games with people he hates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-20T14:43:53-08:00","id":770302,"title":"","content":"I think they need to emphasize more the former aspects with the latter mentioned or alluded to more in passing. Eight paragraphs of his ten-paragraph writeup [before Panoply/Combat Tactics/Domain] are dedicated to his obsessive revenge fantasy, one to his appearance, and one to his actions that aren't &quot;wank about torturing my former circle&quot;. It leaks into the other sections as well; half of his Series Ideas, the first paragraph of his Servants... Eye and Seven Despairs acquires derision not because it's written as &quot;In addition to his horrible deathlord activites of X, Y, and Z, he fetishizes torturing his old circle&quot; but because it's written up as &quot;when not fetishizing torturing his old circle, which he does most of the time as his primary focus, he occasionally deigns to do X, once in a while, when not foisting the responsibility off on a servant so he can enact new cruel dramas on his old circle mates.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T03:37:13-08:00","id":770619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=770196#post770196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Friendly mod warning that there's better words with less baggage than this one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True, loaded choice of words on my part, sorry. Edited that already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T11:09:34-08:00","id":770846,"title":"","content":"For the record, I liked 1e Eye and Seven. In 2e, they turned him into a joke.<br /> <br /> As for workings in general, I feel I should note a couple things, both by the rules and by the story.<br /> <br /> By the rules:<ul><li>Solar Ambition 2 could only hit, say, the Blessed Isle with a curse. Maybe you could get an entire House or lay a curse on the Empress's Bloodline instead, but you're not gonna hit the entire Blessed Isle with one working at Solar Ambition 2.</li> <li>Your Difficulty is going to be increased by 2. So, if you want to do a precise curse that unavoidably causes them problems, you'll be losing 6 successes from your roll.</li> <li>Solars do not currently have any charms that improve their dice rolls for Workings beyond their dice adders. Which means that Lunars might very not have such charms either, so they're going to need to be stunting well to his the same cap.</li> <li>With 20 dice and no tricks, you're averaging ten successes per roll, for 4 net successes towards the goal number of 50. This requires 13 rolls.</li> <li>To get 13 rolls, means that, even if you can get maximum bonuses from complimentary abilities, spells, and components, you're still going to need 3 Means from Cooperation, Time, and Infrastructure. The Realm is actively preventing Lunars from building Infrastructure and, even if you can talk a bunch of Lunar Sorcerers into helping you, that only adds 2. Which means you're going to be spending a month per roll, so this going to take you 13 months, almost a year.</li> <li>Anyone in the targeted area gets to make a reflexive diff 3 Occult roll to notice the impending Working. Someone in the Realm will notice and then they will alert people.</li> <li>If you fail on any roll, that counts as a botch for the purpose of messing with the working. Accepting lesser Finesse will similarly lead to less control over the Working.</li> </ul><br /> In short, if a group of Lunar Sorcerers tried this, they would be painting a big-ass target on themselves and the Working would almost certainly get disrupted by a Sidereal or DB hit squad, assuming the Lunars didn't just get slagged by a pillar of fire from the Realm Defense Grid. Even if they didn't, the Working is almost certainly not going to go exactly as planned, either by a failure or two on a roll or by accepting lesser finesse.<br /> <br /> By the Story, brewing a curse like this should be a numinous thing, involving lots of research and casting. As has been noted, it shouldn't just be a cruse missile you can pull out and just toss around, it should be something weird and cool, with odd clauses. There should not be a possible working that is just &quot;Destroy the Area with Fire.&quot; I also feel I should note that, Salina, even with access to the First Age infrastructure, still needed a team of other Sorcerers to pull off her famous Working and she didn't do it instantly either. Really, the intended narrative role for big workings is that they're there for the evil Sorcerer to try to enact and the heroic PCs to show up to disrupt.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, if you<i> want</i> a cruise missile, go check out the Celestial Spells. Summoning Octavian and ordering him to go destroy the Imperial City of the Realm is much less likely to get you killed than trying to do this via Working and will have a better chance of success at doing some damage than your failed Working ever will.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Deathlords, we don't know just how powerful they are, but, if the Great Contagion was a Working, then the Dowager was working on that thing for something like 300 years and it still didn't destroy Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T11:28:43-08:00","id":770860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=770846#post770846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]To get 13 rolls, means that, even if you can get maximum bonuses from complimentary abilities, spells, and components, you're still going to need 3 Means from Cooperation, Time, and Infrastructure. The Realm is actively preventing Lunars from building Infrastructure and, even if you can talk a bunch of Lunar Sorcerers into helping you, that only adds 2. Which means you're going to be spending a month per roll, so this going to take you 13 months, almost a year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirteen <i>years</i>, not months. It's three months per interval by default if you reach a circle above your capabilities, or a year per interval if you're getting one extra means via time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T16:17:14-08:00","id":771034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/767450-how-have-the-deathlords-not-won-ex3-solar-sorcerous-workings?p=770860#post770860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thirteen <i>years</i>, not months. It's three months per interval by default if you reach a circle above your capabilities, or a year per interval if you're getting one extra means via time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Missed that. Thanks.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. You can't hit the entire Realm with anything short of a Solar 3 Working. A Solar 2 Working will take you a horrendously long time and people will find you and stop you before you finish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}